# Copy to .env. main.py and mock_llm.py both load it automatically.

# --- Required ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Which endpoint the app talks to ---
# Default: the local mock server (start it with `uv run mock_llm.py`)
OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1
# Live OpenAI API — comment out the line above and uncomment this one
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# --- Mock server ---
DELAY_SECONDS=2
# RECORDINGS=recordings/gpt-4o-mini
# PORT=8000

# --- Failure scenarios ---
# ANALYSIS_STATUS / RESPONSE_STATUS take one HTTP status per attempt,
# comma-separated, then cycle. Restart the mock server after changing them.
#
# "requests" = how many the mock serves for one `uv run main.py 1041`.
# The app only ever makes two calls; anything above that is the OpenAI SDK
# retrying on its own, which it does twice for 429 and 5xx but never for 4xx.
#
# Keep sequences to 3 entries or fewer — that is the SDK's whole budget
# (1 try + 2 retries). Longer sequences make consecutive runs differ.

# 1. Healthy. 2 requests, succeeds.                                     [ACTIVE]
#ANALYSIS_STATUS=200
#RESPONSE_STATUS=200

# 2. Call 2 flaky, recovers. 4 requests, succeeds.
#    Retries save the run — and the code still shows only one call.
ANALYSIS_STATUS=200
RESPONSE_STATUS=500,500,200

# 3. Call 2 down, retries exhausted. 4 requests, fails: InternalServerError.
#    Identical cost to scenario 2, opposite outcome. Call 1's analysis was
#    paid for and is thrown away.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=200
# RESPONSE_STATUS=500

# 4. Call 2 rejected outright. 2 requests, fails: BadRequestError.
#    No retries at all — a 4xx is not retryable, so it fails instantly.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=200
# RESPONSE_STATUS=400

# 5. Call 1 rate limited, recovers. 3 requests, succeeds.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=429,200
# RESPONSE_STATUS=200

# 6. Call 1 rate limited, exhausted. 3 requests, fails: RateLimitError.
#    Call 2 never runs, so there is no reply to lose.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=429
# RESPONSE_STATUS=200

# 7. Both calls flaky, both recover. 4 requests, succeeds.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=503,200
# RESPONSE_STATUS=503,200

# 8. Quota exhausted part-way through, and a decision that does not survive.
#    Call 1 succeeds and is paid for; Call 2 hits a 429 carrying
#    code=insufficient_quota, which STICKY_STATUS latches for that model — so
#    gpt-4o-mini returns it for everything from then on, across restarts, while
#    claude-opus-5 keeps working. A 429 says "transient" but insufficient_quota
#    is terminal, so the SDK's 3 attempts are wasted before the app sees it.
#
#    The app then handles it correctly on its own: it falls back to Anthropic and
#    finishes the ticket. Run it and let it finish to see that.
#
#    The point is what a crash costs in the FALLBACK_PAUSE_SECONDS window between
#    deciding and acting. Ctrl+C there, then run it again:
#      run 1: analysis 200, 3x 429, DECISION  -> Ctrl+C during the pause
#      run 2: 3x 429 on the analysis it already had, then redoes it on Anthropic
#    5 calls after the crash, 1 of them work that had not already been done.
#    Restart the mock server to clear the latch.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=200
# RESPONSE_STATUS=429
# STICKY_STATUS=429
# FALLBACK_PAUSE_SECONDS=5

# 9. Gateway failure, for the durable-retry demo. A 504 is retried but never
#    recovers, so both runs fail — the only thing that differs is whether the
#    retry budget was honoured. Ctrl+C the app once `retry` reaches 4 or so,
#    then run it again: in the mock log `retry` restarts at 0 while `seen`
#    keeps climbing. The app lost its count; the upstream did not.
#    MAX_RETRIES is an APP setting (the OpenAI client's budget). The mock never
#    reads it — it only ever sees the requests that budget produces.
# ANALYSIS_STATUS=200
# RESPONSE_STATUS=504
# MAX_RETRIES=10

# --- Optional ---
# MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# MAX_RETRIES=2               # app-side retry budget; 0 disables retrying entirely
# FALLBACK_PAUSE_SECONDS=5    # app-side wait before failing over to a second
#                             # provider. Scenario 8 asks you to Ctrl+C in it, so
#                             # raise it on a projector.

# Only needed if you re-add the Claude recorder script
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
